      "notes": "The verdict is well-structured and evidence-grounded. The 'worsens/moderate/low-confidence' direction is supported by documented cost overruns (E26, E30), the abandoned Wylfa Newydd precedent (E3), and real committed public expenditure (E4, E7). The RAB caveat is correctly handled as a mitigant that shifts rather than eliminates burden. Tier integrity is sound: E3 is correctly labelled measurable (historical fact of abandonment), E26/E30/E35/E44 are projected/institutional forecasts correctly tiered as projected. The E7 'measurable' claim warrants a minor caution \u2014 the \u00a32.5bn figure comes partly from gov.wales/advocacy sources and may be a projected investment figure rather than a confirmed spend, but it is presented as 'initial investment' which is close enough to stated commitment. No party-blind issues; the rationale judges the policy on modelled fiscal effect without attributing motive. The false-balance check passes: direction is 'worsens' not mixed, and the evidence genuinely leans that way. No magnitude or timing violations detected."
